#. translators: %d: days a refused submission is kept
#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:122
#, php-format
msgid "The forms of this site are checked for spam on this server, with no external service, no cookie and no IP address kept. The check keeps daily counts of the submissions by form and by outcome, with nothing of who sent them. To tell spam from legitimate messages, it keeps counts on hashes of the words of the subject and the message of the submissions marked as spam or not spam: no text is kept in them, and nothing ties these counts to a person. The rating the filter gives and the reason for a refusal are stored with the comment or the entry they concern, and deleted with it. A refused submission keeps its subject and its message, without the name or the email address of the sender, for a moderator to review; that message may hold personal details the sender wrote in it. It is deleted %d days after it was last sent."
msgstr ""

